rl":"https://www.meetup.com/markham-weekday-badminton-meetup-group/events/316772978/","description":"**Event Cost :** **$10** per person, ( including one piece of brand new standard feather birdie.)\n**Racquets :** Bring your own racquet. Rentals are available at the club if needed.\n**Shoes :** Please bring indoor gym shoes and change into them at the club before entering the courts.\n**This is a casual meetup group for people in the Markham or Scarborough to play 2 hours morning badminton to pursue your ultimate healthy life! Free sign up and all skill levels are welcome!!**","startDate":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Tiger badminton","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Markham","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"7755 warden ave, Unit 7, Markham, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"GTA Weekday Badminton","url":"https://www.meetup.com/markham-weekday-badminton-meetup-group/"},"performer":"GTA Weekday Badminton"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beginner Drop-In Pickleball – $18/1.5hrs – Register to Secure Your Spot!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/events/316567968/","description":"🏓 **Registration & Payment (Required in Advance):**\nRSVP on Meetup does *not* guarantee your spot.\nTo play, you must register and pay in advance through our registration system.\n👉 **[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=kLGNZre)**\n📞 Or call: 416-924-6211 ext. 0\n**Limited to 18 players.** Once full, no additional players will be admitted.\n\n***\n\n**Beginner Drop-In Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC**\nNew to pickleball? We’ve got the perfect session for you!\nJoin us for **Beginner Drop-In Pickleball** at the Miles Nadal JCC — a welcoming and supportive environment for those just getting started with the game. Whether you're still learning the rules or building confidence on the court, this is a great opportunity to play, practice, and meet fellow beginners.\n\n***\n\n🏓 **Event Details:**\n**Location:** 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through the Spadina doors)\n**Check-In:** Please check in with security and stop by the front desk upon arrival.\n\n***\n\n🏓 **What to Expect:**\n\n* Designed for **beginner-level players** with some familiarity with the rules and scoring\n* Equipment available: borrow paddles and balls with a $20 cash deposit + valid ID\n* Friendly rotations so everyone gets a chance to play\n* Supportive and inclusive environment — no pressure, just fun and learning!\n\n***\n\nCome ready to move, meet new people, and improve your game one rally at a time. We look forward to seeing you on the court!","startDate":"2026-10-05T15:45:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Drop-In Pickleball (3.0+) – $18/1.5hrs – Register to Secure Your Spot!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/events/316569016/","description":"**🏓 Registration & Payment (Required in Advance):**\n**RSVP on Meetup does *not* reserve your spot.**\nTo participate in Drop-In Play, you must register and pay in advance via our registration system.\n👉 **[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=yJJNJ6a)**\n📞 Or register by phone: 416-924-6211 ext. 0\nSpace is limited to **6 players** on a first-come, first-served basis. Once full, no additional participants can be accommodated.\n\\*\\*\\*\n**Drop-In Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC**\nCome play one of the fastest-growing sports in North America — right in the heart of the Annex!\nJoin us for friendly, active Pickleball at the Miles Nadal JCC, just steps from Spadina Station. It’s a great way to stay active, meet new people, and have some fun!\n\\*\\*\\*\n**🏓 Event Details:**\n**Location:** 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through the Spadina doors)\n**Check-In:** Stop by security and check in at the front desk when you arrive.\n\\*\\*\\*\n**🏓 Other Info:**\n\n* Paddles and balls are available for loan at the front desk with a **$20 cash deposit and valid ID**\n* This session is intended for **intermediate players and above** — participants should have a solid understanding of Pickleball rules, scoring, and gameplay, and be comfortable with consistent rallies and court positioning\n* Courts are rotated regularly so everyone gets a chance to play\n* Welcoming, inclusive environment\n\n\\*\\*\\*\nCome ready to rally, socialize, and have a great time on the court. We can’t wait to see you there!","startDate":"2026-10-05T17:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"NEW TIME!! FREE Spanish, English, and French Oral Conversational Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/events/316770437/","description":"\\*These classes are not a language exchange, but instead are meant to be a step in between so that students feel confident maintaining in depth and grammatically correct oral conversations outside of class\\*\n\n\\***Meetup event numbers only tend to show new students registering and do not include returning students attending class.**\\* \\*Per class, there is an average of 7 students. \\*\\*The first 2 classes are free and then only cost between 18 and 35 depending on which type of class you want to continue with\\*\n\nThese French, English (For Spanish and French speakers only), and Spanish classes are primarily meant for adults who are travellers, or who are planning to live in a French, English, or Spanish-speaking country. The classes are primarily oral-based through guided conversations. They will teach you how to handle conversations in situations such as **\"Going to the Convenience Store\"**, **\"Making Plans\"**, **\"Negotiating Prices\"**, and **\"Going out for a Drink\"**. To ensure that students get used to using the language automatically, students will learn to maintain contextual conversations with timing before moving on to the next lesson. Call (647)787-9953, e-mail us info@monkeylingo.ca, or visit monkeylingo.ca for more information! **Online and private classes are also available!**\n\nNo other language classes are as conversational as these ones. We guarantee it! Cheap parking can be found using the \"Spot Hero\" app.","startDate":"2026-10-05T20:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"600 Bay St.","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"600 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/"},"performer":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free English Classes  - in-person at our Toronto school ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-jpellpgf/events/316572051/","description":"Practise your English in a friendly, welcoming class in Toronto.\nJoin our free in-person English class and improve your speaking, fluency, grammar and vocabulary with supportive teachers. This class is a great opportunity to practise English, build confidence and meet new people.\n\n**When**\nEvery weekday Monday - Friday\n2.00pm–4.00pm\n\n**Where**\nTeaching House Toronto\nOHC / Sol Camps\n469 Jarvis St\nToronto, ON M4Y 2G8\nCanada\n\n[REGISTER NOW](https://4i4d9.share.hsforms.com/2GTDQYBIjRTmHonHUe_WuLQ)\n\n**What you’ll practise**\n\n* Speaking and fluency\n* Grammar and vocabulary\n* Listening and pronunciation\n* Everyday English for real-life situations\n* Confidence using English with other people\n\n**Who can join?**\nAdults aged 18+ who want to improve their English. Refugees, asylum seekers and newcomers are very welcome.\n\n**About the classes**\nThe classes are taught by trainee English teachers on a Cambridge-accredited CELTA course and supervised by experienced teacher trainers.\n\n**Cost**\nFree\n\n**Before the class**\nPlease arrive a little early so we can welcome you and check your English level.\nSpaces may be limited, so please RSVP if you would like to attend.Cost: FREE\n\nSign up using this [registration form ](https://4i4d9.share.hsforms.com/2GTDQYBIjRTmHonHUe_WuLQ)for automatic reminders and to be on our list for future classes.","startDate":"2026-10-05T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Teaching House Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"469 Jarvis St, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"FREE English classes in Toronto, Canada","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-jpellpgf/"},"performer":"FREE English classes in Toronto, Canada"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Monday Game Nights at LVLUP GAMES!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/m-b-g-u/events/316762546/","description":"We invite you to join us to play games and socialize!\n\n**There is now a cut off for RSVPs. If you do not RSVP for an event on meetup, we cannot guarantee that we will have a seat available.**\n\nCAFE POLICIES\n\n1. There is an entry fee of 6/person + tax for this event. If you do not RSVP at least 4 hours prior to the event start on the day, the price will be 8+ tax. You must check in and pay upon arrival.\n\n3. We are a cafe and do not permit outside food and drink (water bottles excluded). However, you may bring food in from the other food businesses (Henry's, Vito's, not the convenience store) in the plaza to support our neighbours\n\n5. Stay within the designated tables. We may have other events, reservations and walk-ins; we need to keep other tables clear in order to be able to best assess our seating capacity at all times. DO NOT REARRANGE TABLES WITHOUT CONSENT FROM STAFF\n\n7. Be considerate of other guests when selecting games from our library and limit the number of games you bring back to each table to two (2) at a time\n\n9. You are welcome to bring your own games to use in the cafe, but LVLUP GAMES is not responsible for lost, stolen, or otherwise damaged games/components\n\nAlso as a general meet up rule, to be considerate to other guests. Since we have limited seating, it is of the utmost importance that if you plan on attending you sign up for the event. Likewise, if you are unable to make it, kindly mark that you will not be coming so your spot becomes available for another per\n\nWe appreciate your understanding and cooperation. Hope to see you soon!","startDate":"2026-10-05T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"LVLUP GAMES","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"833 Westlock Rd Unit #9, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Mississauga Board Gamers United","url":"https://www.meetup.com/m-b-g-u/"},"performer":"Mississauga Board Gamers United"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Together Toronto and YC Winter 2027 (W27) Application Session","url":"https://www.meetup.com/techto/events/316492775/","description":"**This is a paid event. You must register and have a ticket to attend.** 👉 **[Together Toronto and YC Winter 2027 (W27) Application Session](https://luma.com/together-toronto-october-2026)**\n\n**Together Toronto - the stories behind how companies actually get built here.**\n\nThe stories that actually shape how companies get built in this city rarely make it onto a stage. This one's different.\n\nTogether Toronto is TechTO's signature gathering for founders, operators, builders, and investors who want more than inspiration - they want the real playbook. Real founders. Honest conversations about what it took to launch, scale, and survive Toronto's tech scene.\n\nWhether you're building your first company, scaling a team, or figuring out what's next - this is the event worth showing up for.\n\n**You'll leave with:**\n\n* Founder stories with the specifics left in\n* Connections with the people building what's next\n* Conversations that challenge how you think about your own company\n\n📅 Monday\\, Oct 5\\| 6PM\\- 9PM\n📍 Downtown Toronto\n🎟️ Paid event \\- tickets required \\| Free for TechTO Members\n\n**Register via Luma:** [https://luma.com/together-toronto-october-2026](https://luma.com/together-toronto-october-2026)","startDate":"2026-10-05T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"U of T: Schwartz Reisman Innovation Campus","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto, ON","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"108 College St, Toronto, ON, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"TechTO","url":"https://www.meetup.com/techto/"},"performer":"TechTO"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Introduction to Entrepreneurship: Is This for Me, and Where Do I Start?","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-public-library-small-business-networking-meetup/events/316714288/","description":"Most people don't hesitate because their idea is bad. They hesitate because they think entrepreneurship is intimidating. This opening session challenges this assumption by using real Canadian statistics and introducing the Business Model Canvas, both of which can help you capture how a business creates value, reaches customers, and generates capital. By the end of this session, you will be given a chance to start filling in your own Business Model Canvas and a chance to network with other participants.\n\nThe program includes a short networking component, providing participants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs.\n\nPresented by Ryan Knight, TPL's 2026 [Entrepreneur in Residence](https://tpl.ca/programs-and-classes/featured/entrepreneur-in-residence/) (EIR) at Toronto Reference Library.\n\n**Registration via TPL website:** [https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31](https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31)\n**Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached.**\n\nAccessibility\nLive or automated closed captioning, sign language interpretation, intervenor services, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to: [tpl.ca/accessibility-events](https://tpl.ca/accessibility/accessibility-supports/programs-and-events/?_gl=1*v83hy7*_ga*NDk5MDg2NTE1LjE3NjYwMDgxODQ.*_ga_G99DMMNG39*czE3NjkxMDY3NDMkbzE0JGcxJHQxNzY5MTA2ODM0JGozOCRsMCRoMA..).","startDate":"2026-10-05T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Public Library - Toronto Reference Library","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"789 Yonge St, Toronto, ON M4W 2G8, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Public Library Small Business Networking Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-public-library-small-business-networking-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto Public Library Small Business Networking Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Sweat & Tone Class","url":"https://www.meetup.com/sweat-tone-group-fitness/events/316765644/","description":"Want to start your week strong?\n\nJoin us every Monday for a 50-minute, music-driven, full-body workout combining cardio bursts, mat-based strength work, and core training. Inspired by the precision and controlled movements of barre, this workout will leave you feeling open and energized.\n\nStarting September 28th at 6 pm. Just bring your mat and be ready to move. All fitness levels are welcome.\n\nLocation:\nDance Annex studio 509a\n509 Bloor St W 2nd Floor,\nToronto, ON M5S 1Y2\n\nPlease register here to attend: https://danastrainingto.simplybook.me/v2/\n\nEmail danastrainingTO@gmail.com with any questions.","startDate":"2026-10-05T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"509 Bloor Street West","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"509 Bloor St W, Toronto, ON M5S 1Y2, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Sweat & Tone Group Fitness","url":"https://www.meetup.com/sweat-tone-group-fitness/"},"performer":"Sweat & Tone Group Fitness"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Boxing Fundamentals (16+) — Build Strength & Skill | Fall 2026 Session","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-martial-arts-archery-dance/events/316572831/","description":"**Fall 2026 Session**\n**Registration required in advance**\n**[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=y2pwW29)**\n☎️ Or call **416-924-6211 ext. 0**\n\n️ **Fees**\n• Full program session registration available\n• Prorated pricing if joining after the start date\n• Drop-in options may be available (space permitting)\n**Boxing Fundamentals (16+) at the Miles Nadal JCC**\n\nReady to build strength, sharpen your skills, and break a sweat? This no-contact beginner program introduces essential boxing fundamentals including stance, footwork, punches, bagwork, partner drills, and conditioning — all in a supportive and inclusive environment. No sparring involved.\n\nPerfect for new boxers or anyone looking to develop a strong foundation while improving fitness and confidence.\n\n**Led by Coach Nick Radionov — former Ukrainian National Olympic Boxing Team member, Level 3 Boxing Ontario–certified coach, and multi-time world kickboxing champion.**\n\n**Program Details**\n**Location:** Miles Nadal JCC — 750 Spadina Ave. (enter via Spadina doors)\n\n**What You’ll Learn & Benefit From**\n**Learn the Basics** — Develop proper form, movement, and striking technique\n**Build Strength & Stamina** — High-energy conditioning in every class\n**Train with Confidence** — Beginner-friendly instruction in a welcoming environment\n**Hands-On Skill Development** — Bagwork & partner drills (no-contact/no sparring)\n\n**What to Bring:** Handwraps, boxing gloves, indoor athletic shoes, and a water bottle.\n\nJoin us and build skill, strength, and confidence — one round at a time!","startDate":"2026-10-05T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave, Room 317b, M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Downtown Toronto Martial Arts & Dance","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-martial-arts-archery-dance/"},"performer":"Downtown Toronto Martial Arts & Dance"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"FREE Spanish, English, and French Oral Conversational Class 4 Adults","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/events/316572443/","description":"\\*These classes are not a language exchange, but instead are meant to be a step in between so that students feel confident maintaining in depth and grammatically correct oral conversations outside of class\\*\n\n\\***Meetup event numbers only tend to show new students registering and do not include returning students attending class.** **Per class, there is an average of 7 students.** The first 2 classes are free and then only cost between $18 and $35 depending on which type of class you want to continue with\\*\n\nThese French, English (For Spanish and French speakers only), and Spanish classes are primarily meant for adults who are travellers, or who are planning to live in a French, English, or Spanish-speaking country. The classes are primarily oral-based through guided conversations. They will teach you how to handle conversations in situations such as **\"Going to the Convenience Store\"**, **\"Making Plans\"**, **\"Negotiating Prices\"**, and **\"Going out for a Drink\"**. To ensure that students get used to using the language automatically, students will learn to maintain contextual conversations with timing before moving on to the next lesson. Call (647)787-9953, e-mail us info@monkeylingo.ca, or visit monkeylingo.ca for more information! **Online and private classes are also available!**\n\nNo other language classes are as conversational as these ones. We guarantee it! Cheap parking can be found using the \"Spot Hero\" app.","startDate":"2026-10-05T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"600 Bay St.","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"600 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/"},"performer":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beginner's Swimming Workshop","url":"https://www.meetup.com/alexswimschool-meetup-group/events/316725491/","description":"Dive into the world of swimming with our exciting meetup group! Join us for a beginner-friendly workshop as we cover essential skills and techniques to feel confident swimming. Our experienced instructors will provide tips on breathing, sighting, and navigation to help you conquer any body of water. Whether you're new to swimming or looking to brush up on your skills, this workshop is the perfect opportunity to enhance your abilities in a supportive and encouraging environment. Don't miss out on this chance to explore the excitement of swimming with our welcoming community of swimmers.\n\nAdmission includes a 1 hour swimming lesson, group or individual, depending on your comfort level and ability. All lessons will begin at the start of each hour (i.e. 6 pm, 7 pm). You are encouraged to arrive 10-15 minutes early to get acquainted, as well as change & set up.\n\nThis is a BYOE workshop (Bring Your Own Equipment), so bathing suits, bathing caps, goggles, and ear/nose plugs are your responsibility. All other equipment, such as floatation devices, are available on site.\n\nI will be on site to guide you through the process and answer any questions you might have, as well as collect admission fees. You are welcome to hang back after your lesson to observe (a large viewing gallery above the pool is available, however please be respectful of participants & instructors that are in session). This is a public pool facility, so please follow all safety protocols (i.e. no running on deck)\n\nWith that in mind, I look forward to seeing you all out there and ready to have a blast in the pool.","startDate":"2026-10-05T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","ev